  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Building Community Resilience and Delivery of Essential services for vulnerable children and women in Maguindanao, Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. More young children, adolescent boys and girls, pregnant and lactating women, especially the teenagers, in the selected communities have access to health, nutrition and WASH services and practice positive behavior in the early learning and alternative learning systems both in development and humanitarian contexts 2. Children, adolescents boys and girls and youth have increased access to quality early childhood education and alternative learning system services including in humanitarian crisis 3. An inclusive and equitable child protection system is in place and used to prevent and respond to violence in all settings including humanitarian crisis 4. Child friendly provincial, city and municipal planning and investment for children&apos;s rights, young people empowered, and reduced disaster risks in all local governments during humanitarian crisis</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">High community resilience, coverage of essential services for children, adolescents, and women in the selected conflict-affected and/or remote municipalities of Maguindanao del Norte, Maguindanao del Sur province and Cotabato City, BARM1. 2026&#xb144;&#xae4c;&#xc9c0; &#xc601;&#xc720;&#xc544;, &#xccad;&#xc18c;&#xb144;, &#xc784;&#xc2e0; &#xbc0f; &#xc218;&#xc720;&#xc911;&#xc778; &#xc18c;&#xb140;&#xb4e4;&#xc744; &#xc704;&#xd55c; &#xbcf4;&#xac74; &#xc704;&#xc0dd; &#xc601;&#xc591; &#xc2dd;&#xc218; &#xc704;&#xd589; &#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4; &#xc811;&#xadfc;&#xc131;&#xacfc; &#xac74;&#xac15; &#xd589;&#xc704; &#xc2e4;&#xcc9c; &#xd5a5;&#xc0c1; 2. 2025&#xb144; &#xb9d0;&#xae4c;&#xc9c0; &#xbaa8;&#xb4e0; &#xc5b4;&#xb9b0;&#xc774;&#xc640; &#xccad;&#xc18c;&#xb144;&#xc744; &#xc704;&#xd55c; &#xc591;&#xc9c8;&#xc758; &#xc720;&#xc544;&#xbcf4;&#xc721; &#xbc0f; &#xbc1c;&#xb2ec;&#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4; &#xbc0f; &#xb300;&#xccb4; &#xd559;&#xc2b5; &#xc2dc;&#xc2a4;&#xd15c;(ALS) &#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4; &#xc774;&#xc6a9; 3. 2027&#xb144; &#xb9d0;&#xae4c;&#xc9c0; &#xc544;&#xb3d9; &#xbcf4;&#xd638;, &#xc0ac;&#xd68c; &#xbcf5;&#xc9c0; &#xc2dc;&#xc2a4;&#xd15c; &#xbc0f; &#xc9c0;&#xbc29; &#xc815;&#xbd80; &#xb2e8;&#xc704;&#xc5d0;&#xc11c; LGU&#xbcc4; &#xc6b0;&#xc120;&#xc21c;&#xc704;&#xc5d0; &#xb530;&#xb978; &#xc704;&#xd5d8;&#xc5d0; &#xcc98;&#xd55c; &#xc544;&#xb3d9;, &#xccad;&#xc18c;&#xb144;, &#xccad;&#xb144;, &#xac00;&#xc871; &#xbc0f; &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed; &#xc0ac;&#xd68c; &#xac15;&#xd654; &#xbc0f; &#xbcf4;&#xd638;&#xb97c; &#xc704;&#xd55c; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9; &#xac15;&#xd654;  4. &#xc544;&#xb3d9;&#xad8c;&#xb9ac; &#xb0b4;&#xc6a9;&#xc744; &#xbc18;&#xc601;&#xd558;&#xc5ec; &#xb370;&#xc774;&#xd130;&#xb97c; &#xae30;&#xbc18;&#xc73c;&#xb85c; &#xc9c0;&#xc5ed; &#xc815;&#xbd80;&#xc758; &#xc815;&#xcc45; &#xbc0f; &#xc608;&#xc0b0; &#xc218;&#xb9bd;</narrative>
